        "id": 40329,
        "name": "faust",
        "username": "faust",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/c89c15/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-10-30T23:53:47.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"lugaru\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lugaru/48/2767_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> lugaru:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Gnipp wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Am I missing where you can change the portrait image on a hero card?i see where you can do this on other cards, but not on the Hero Card front.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nI was playing around this morning and was not able to figure it out either, maybe it was ommited?\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It looks like its hiding behind another button. Must have just got messed up when I converted all the properties panes to relative values. I've nearly finished the environment deck so I'll release v0.5 this week with this fixed.</p>\n<p>In the meantime, its under the 'Change Power Color' button. Click in the hero name field then press shift+tab to cycle backwards through buttons. You can press space to select the button once you have tabbed to the button under Change Power Color.</p>\n<p>I'll try and release v0.5 tomorrow or Thursday.</p>",
