        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/43a26b/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-11-14T18:59:48.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"lugaru\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lugaru/48/2767_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> lugaru:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Nice, at this point all I'm looking for is a custom Villain card… right now I have screenshots and did the front and back for a new Voss but I dont have a card to put his front and back rules on. Also (and Koga should consider this too) an Oversized Villain card template would rock… something with 2 layers so you can have a full body image that is half obscured by the rules and advanced edition info.&nbsp;Also I started a custom enviroment deck, well… started taking screenshots for it. It is inspired by the Tomb of Anubis… this one is the Megalopolis Prison with about 10 unique super powered prisoners (in orange jump suits), a tough warden, and facility cards (generators, walls) that must be protected to stop the prison break.It should be a fun deck to play with guys like Ambuscade or any of the Rook City villains who would benefit from a Prison Break. I'm contemplating making two prisoners into Citizens (Citizen Hit and Citizen Run) but that could create shenanigans with the Citizen Dawn deck.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>This sounds fantastic.&nbsp; You could have a few different prisoners with key words…these two are citizens, this is a thug, this is a minion, etc.&nbsp; Very cool options you could have.&nbsp; But whether you go there or not this is just plain cool.</p>",
