      {
        "id": 40344,
        "name": "plasticbrain",
        "username": "plasticbrain",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/plasticbrain/{size}/2658_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-11-27T18:30:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p><strong>EDIT 11/28/12:</strong> i found a way to change the color of the Quote bubble (simply find it in the FOTM image file, open it with GIMP, and change its color there; fortunately, it works retroactively on any cards you'ved created and saved when you re-open them!). so, i've removed that from the list below, though i would still recommend re-coloring it for future iterations of this software package. i've added the little bug about the \"card text\" box removing paragraph returns to the list.</p><p>@faust:</p><p>first, thanks for creating this card editor! it's a fun tool to have.</p><p>here are my suggestions to make it better:</p><p>1) be able to <strong>copy </strong>a card (not increase the number). this is so you don't have to edit <em>every single field</em> to get your cards to look the same when you want to use fonts and colors than the default ones. so frustrating!</p><p>2) be able to change the order of cards at will. so for example, if you create a new one-shot later for your deck, you can move it up to sit with the other one-shots.</p><p>3) might be nice if on the preview page, for the non-character cards, a preview of the card's text (or just the first few words) was one of the listed fields. also on this page, it would be nice if the preview picture of the card was at least large enough to read the text clearly.</p><p>4) finally, two fixes needed:</p><p>&gt;&gt;&gt;a) when you choose \"Export cards as <strong>PNG</strong>\" they export as <strong>JPG </strong>and vice-versa. these somehow got mixed up. the \"Export DECK as...\" ones are fine though.</p><p><strong>&gt;&gt;&gt;b) when you save a deck , if you put paragraph returns between or before any text in the \"card text\" box, they are gone when you re-open it.</strong></p><p>&gt;&gt;&gt;c) you have templates for the Villain's HP card (front&amp;back) but not for their <strong>Gameplay </strong>card (front&amp;back needed for this too). the Gameplay card is actually more important since it tells you how to play with the Villain!</p><p>thanks! i'll be on the lookout for version 6!</p><p>here's what i've started on:</p><p>![](upload://6Fga4OsDVWTJ7rXQRAwYJIRSgXv.jpeg)</p>",
        "post_number": 31,
        "post_type": 1,
